> basis a { inv(x) = ~x }
> basis b : a { andp(x, y) = x & y }
> basis a : b { orp(x, y) = x | y }
> basis self : self { t(x, y) = lut }
> basis l1 { t(x, y) = lut }
> basis l2 : l1 { u(x, y, z) = lut }
> basis l1 : l2 { v(x) = ~x }
> f(a: u1, b: u1) = a | b
> gates f basis a
gates for f: 2 input bits -> 1 output bit, basis a
  minimal: cost 1, 1 step (no program of cost <= 0 exists; 4 candidates searched)
  checked: the program reproduces every output bit on all 4 care inputs
  t0 = orp(a, b)               = a | b
  r0 = t0
> gates f basis self
gates for f: 2 input bits -> 1 output bit, basis self
  minimal: cost 1, 1 step (no program of cost <= 0 exists; 1 candidates searched)
  checked: the program reproduces every output bit on all 4 care inputs
  t0 = t(a, b, 0x0e)                 = (~b & a) | (b & ~a) | (b & a)
  r0 = t0
> gates f basis l1
gates for f: 2 input bits -> 1 output bit, basis l1
